.TH AGENTGUARD-CHURN-BYPASS 1 "2026-09-10" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agentguard-churn-bypass \- manage the edit-churn guard bypass for this session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentguard-churn-bypass on
.RI [ reason ...]
.br
.B agentguard-churn-bypass off
.br
.B agentguard-churn-bypass status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agentguard-churn-bypass
opts the current agent session out of (or back into) the
.BR agent-hook-pre-edit (1)
churn guard, which warns after
.B AGENTGUARD_EDIT_CHURN_WARN
edits to one file and blocks after
.B AGENTGUARD_EDIT_CHURN_BLOCK
edits.
.PP
Hook processes inherit their environment from the agent process, so an
.B export AGENTGUARD_EDIT_CHURN_BYPASS=1
in an agent tool shell never reaches them. This command writes (or
removes) a bypass marker file in the session state dir instead, a
channel the agent can actually use mid-session. The marker resolves
from runtime session ids when present and from the agent parent
process otherwise, so it stays scoped to the current session. Only
one session is ever managed: the first session id with existing
state, or the first session id when no state exists yet. A nested
agent's bypass never touches the outer session. Session ids
containing
.B /
or
.B ..
are rejected. Every session start
.RB ( agent-hook-session-start (1))
removes any leftover marker, so a reused session key never inherits
a previous session's bypass. The bypass is deliberate and opt-in: it
only exists after an explicit
.B on ,
and a new session starts un-bypassed.
.TP
.B on [reason ...]
Bypass the churn warn and block for this session. When no session
state exists yet, the marker is planted under every plausible state
root so the first hook to run finds it.
.TP
.B off
Remove this session's bypass marker from every state root.
.TP
.B status
Show whether the bypass is active and current churn totals.
Exits 0 when bypassed, 1 when not.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; for
.BR status ,
the bypass is active.
.TP
.B 1
Operational failure (no session identity, unwritable state); for
.BR status ,
the bypass is not active.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (missing or unknown subcommand).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-pre-edit (1),
.BR agent-hook-post-edit (1),
.BR agent-hook-session-start (1)
